Summary: winemac: in host mode, the displays and current mode come from the host
Category: graphics
Kind: feature
Feature: embedding
Origin: wine-mac-builds
Upstream: no
Why: With HostWindows (winemac-host-windows) the host shows the program's
 windows, and it may show them on less than the whole screen: Second
 Chance keeps them below a MacBook's notch. Until now the driver still
 took its monitors from NSScreen and its current mode from
 CGDisplayCopyDisplayMode, so Wine thought the screen was the full height,
 and Second Chance needed a helper injected into Wine that changed what
 those calls return. Now, in host mode, the driver asks the host
 (displays_get) when it enumerates the displays: each monitor's rect and
 work area are the host's display, the current mode's size is that
 display's size (refresh rate and depth stay the real mode's), that size
 is listed among the modes, and setting it changes nothing real. A screen
 the host doesn't report is left out. The host's first display must be at
 the protocol's origin; when it isn't, or the host doesn't answer or
 answers unsupported, the driver uses the real displays. A host that
 answers unsupported isn't asked again by that process; one that doesn't
 answer within the call timeout (2 s) is asked again at the next
 enumeration, so a host that was slow once still gets its displays used.
 DISPLAYS_CHANGED from the host already reached Wine's display-change
 handling, which enumerates again. Plain mode is unchanged.
 With tools/wmh-testhost answering 1512x945 (work area 1512x920), a test
 program saw that monitor, work area, current mode and SM_CX/CYSCREEN,
 and after DISPLAYS_CHANGED to 1440x900 it saw 1440x900 throughout.
Programs: Second Chance (an app that embeds Wine): every program shown
 below the notch of a 14" MacBook Pro (1512x945 points there, not
 1512x982).
Enable: see winemac-host-windows (HostWindows and WINEMAC_HOST_SERVICE)
 by a host that answers displays_get
Messages: "host: the first display isn't at the origin (%g,%g); using the
 real displays", "host: display %u has no size; using the real displays"
 (warn:macdrv; shown only with WINEDEBUG=warn+macdrv)
Known issues: without EmulateModeset, the real modes are still listed and
 can be set, including ones taller than the host's display.
Uncertain: Host displays are matched to real screens: the first to the
 primary, the others by overlap with the real screen's rect. Without
 EmulateModeset: after the host's display changed (1512x945 to 1440x900
 in the test host), Wine logged "No matching mode found 1512x945x32 @60"
 once, most likely restoring the test program's temporary
 (CDS_FULLSCREEN) mode at exit, a size the display no longer had; nothing
 visible came of it. Not tested with a real host: a real display
 rearrangement (DISPLAYS_CHANGED), clicks, or RetinaMode.
Docs: docs/app-embedded-protocol.md
Expects before it: winemac-host-windows; it extends cocoa_host.m and
 cocoa_host.h, which winemac-host-windows creates
Status: 11.22: 2026-11-26: a displays_get that timed out (or failed) is
 retried at the next enumeration; only "unsupported" stops the process
 asking. Not yet in a build.
 11.22: 2026-11-22: confirmed by Second Chance on a 14" MacBook Pro
 (macOS 15.6.1), host16 with no Wine helpers loaded: Wine saw 1512x945,
 and a popup over the primary monitor filled the screen up to the notch.
 host16 also passed Second Chance's full hosted integration run on meeka.
 11.22: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T002454 and T025644 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed

